Check split's NAME_MAX limit against the file name, not the whole path.
The prefix may include a directory, and its length counted toward the
255-byte limit on the name of a piece, so a prefix in a deep directory
failed with "suffix too long". Measure only the last component.

---
 coreutils/split.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/split.c
+++ b/coreutils/split.c
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
 		argv[0] = (char *) bb_msg_standard_input;
 	}
 
-	if (NAME_MAX < strlen(sfx) + suffix_len)
+	if (NAME_MAX < strlen(bb_basename(sfx)) + suffix_len)
 		bb_simple_error_msg_and_die("suffix too long");
 
 	{
